FILE templates/ledger-controlled-file-delivery/README.md
# Controlled file delivery Ledger pattern

Read [Actions and transactions](../../references/capabilities/actions-and-transactions.md) and [Connectors](../../references/capabilities/connectors.md) before authoring this pattern; they contain the bounded controlled-file contract shipped with this Skill. Declare `{{email_connection}}` as an `email/smtp` connection whose current detail publishes the asynchronous write operation `send_file_email`.

```json
{
  "actions": {
    "{{controlled_file_owner}}.deliver_file": {
      "kind": "record_operation",
      "handler": {
        "reason": "The business record update and controlled delivery intent must commit atomically",
        "access": {
          "{{controlled_file_owner}}": ["get_for_update", "conditional_update"]
        },
        "file_operations": ["verify_clean"],
        "connector_calls": {
          "{{email_connection}}": "send_file_email"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

`verify_clean` semantics, `queued`≠`sent`, and `unavailable`/`manual_handoff_required` fail-closed rules are owned by the two documents above; model delivery status/evidence separately from business audit.
